WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.460
If you’re a fan of Frozen, you’ll be looking
forward to the short film Frozen Fever, showing

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.200
in front of the new live-action Cinderella.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.839
In this video I’m going to be running through
my favourite moments from the new short

00:00:12.839 --> 00:00:20.279
So if you haven’t seen Frozen Fever yet,
this video does contain spoilers!

00:00:20.279 --> 00:00:26.019
Frozen Fever features another insanely catchy
song from Robert Lopez and Kristen Anderson-Lopez,

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:30.359
the husband-and-wife song-writing team behind
the mega hit songs from Frozen.

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:35.340
The new song is called "Making Today A Perfect
Day" so get prepared to hear it everywhere

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.120
on constant repeat!

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.949
Speaking of songs, I loved the little call-back
in Frozen Fever to Frozen’s monster hit

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:47.820
Let It Go, after Elsa makes a new dress for
Anna, with just a flick of her wrist.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:53.270
Anna’s worried about Elsa having a cold,
but Elsa simply replies ‘A cold never bothered

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.109
me anyway’.

00:00:56.109 --> 00:00:59.769
Never has having a cold been as much fun as
it is in Frozen Fever!

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:03.770
Because when Elsa sneezes, out pop adorable
little snowmen!

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:07.200
And the more she sneezes, the more tiny snowmen
appear!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.110
Olaf certainly loves having a bunch of little
brothers!

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.130
Elsa’s put in a lot of effort to make the
first birthday she and Anna have celebrated

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.130
together as perfect as possible.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:20.320
But all those snowmen running wild around
the palace, creating havoc, are getting Elsa

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.410
rather stressed.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:26.510
Still, the look on Anna’s face is an absolute
picture when she sees her birthday party in

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:31.630
the palace courtyard where she finds a pyramid
of little snowmen, with Olaf in the middle

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.250
and Sven and Kristoff on top with a gorgeous
ice cream cake!

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:41.131
And I love the way in all the chaos, the letters
in the “Happy Birthday, Anna” banner get

00:01:41.131 --> 00:01:44.880
changed round so it says “Dry Banana Hippy
Hat”!!

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:51.730
Oh, and I love how Sven puts his antlers to
use cutting up the birthday cake!

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:56.790
When Queen Elsa goes to blow the birthday
bugle, things don’t quite go according to

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.470
plan, but that doesn’t mean that the end
result isn’t perfect!

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.789
So, what happens?

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:08.610
Well, instead of blowing the bugle, Elsa sneezes
into it instead, creating a huge snowball,

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:13.580
which then flies over the sea to the Southern
Isles where it lands on Hans, who’d been

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.540
shovelling horse manure into a cart.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.390
And where does Hans end up?

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.340
Yes, you guessed it, right in that cart full
of manure!

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:25.380
How excited are you to see Frozen Fever?

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.100
And if you’ve seen it, what did you think?

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.910
Who’s your favourite Frozen character?

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.970
And what would you like to see in a feature-length
Frozen sequel?

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:37.020
Let me know in the comments below!

